01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
The Iron Claw is a 2023 biographical sports drama film written and directed by Sean Durkin
about the Von Erichs, a family of professional wrestlers beset by tragedy.

12
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The film depicts the struggles of wrestling company owner Fritz Von Erich's sons to achieve
the success for which their father groomed them, from 1979 to the early 1990s.

13
01:21:42,857 --> 01:21:48,857
The film stars Zac Efron as Kevin Von Erich alongside Jeremy Allen White, Harris Dickinson, Maura
Tierney, Stanley Simons, Holt McCallany, and Lily James as other members of the family.

14
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The title comes from the "Iron Claw", a signature move of the Von
Erichs, which takes on thematic resonance within the film.

15
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The Iron Claw premiered at the Texas Theatre in Dallas on November 8, 2023.

16
01:40:34,285 --> 01:40:40,285
It was released in the United States by A24 on December 22, 2023, and
by Lionsgate in the United Kingdom on February 9, 2024.

17
01:46:51,428 --> 01:46:57,428
It grossed over $45 million, on a $15.9 million budget, and received positive reviews, with Efron's
performance receiving acclaim from critics, who deemed it the best of his career.

18
01:53:08,571 --> 01:53:14,571
It was named one of the top 10 films of 2023 by the National Board of Review.

19
01:59:25,714 --> 01:59:31,714
The film explores themes of suicide, coma, sports, 1970s, texas.

20
